    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2009-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Working outward, \\[ \\begin{aligned} &1 + \\cfrac{1}{1 + \\cfrac{1}{1 + 1}} \\\\ &= 1 + \\cfrac{1}{1 + \\dfrac{1}{2}} \\\\ &= 1 + \\dfrac{1}{\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\ &= 1 + \\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{5}{3}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Simplify from the innermost fraction outward",
        "The inner expression \\(1 + \\dfrac{1}{1+1}\\) equals \\(\\dfrac{3}{2}\\)"
      ],
